module dev.avinlang.marshal

// Which waiting jobs start now. Pure: the daemon hands it what is running and what is waiting, and
// starts what it answers.
//
// - Development jobs share a budget of units and of memory. A job starts when its units and its
//   memory fit beside what is running.
// - The queue is first come, first served: the job at its head is never overtaken by one that would
//   delay it. A later job may start ahead of a head that does not fit only if it fits now AND it is
//   expected to end before the head could start (backfill), so the head starts no later for it.
// - The landing lane holds one landing job at a time: a landing job starts when the lane is free and
//   its memory fits beside what is running, whatever units development jobs hold. Once it runs, its
//   units count against the budget as a development job's do (what it weighs, or what it is measured
//   using where that is more, raised as any job is), so the development jobs after it wait for what
//   it leaves. When its memory does not fit, it drains the machine: nothing else starts, neither a
//   development job (not even as backfill) nor a take-slot waiter, until running jobs have freed
//   enough memory, so the landing job goes next. One whose memory alone exceeds the budget starts
//   when nothing else runs. Its memory is counted, so development jobs make room for it rather than
//   the other way round.
// - The quick lane runs short jobs at once, outside the unit budget: at most `QuickSlots` at a time,
//   in queue order, each when its memory fits beside what is running. Its jobs are decided after the
//   landing lane and before every development job, so a quick job never delays a landing job (one
//   that drains the machine holds the quick lane too) and goes ahead of development jobs. Its memory
//   is counted while it runs; one that waits for memory keeps that memory from development jobs, so
//   it is next to start rather than starved, and the quick jobs behind it wait behind it.
// - What take-slot.zsh holds and waits for (`Outside`) shares the same budget and the same arrival
//   order. Its holders take units and are expected to end at any moment, so nothing backfills behind
//   a head that waits for them; its waiters stand in the queue by arrival time, and one marshal can
//   not start is never overtaken by a marshal job. Take-slot admits only its earliest waiter and
//   only when it fits, so a waiter that fits now holds its units as if it had started, and one behind
//   a blocked head waits.
// - Waiting is bounded (`Fairness`). Priorities put later jobs ahead of earlier ones, and each that
//   fits starts, so a big job could wait for ever while small ones keep starting. The first
//   development job in queue order that has waited `afterMs` goes ahead of every other development
//   job not in the urgent band; when it does not fit, the machine drains for it. The urgent band goes
//   ahead of it: while a development job in the band waits, the first of them in queue order takes the
//   drain over, and the job past the bound waits for it among the jobs not in the band; once no urgent
//   job waits, the drain is that job's again. The landing and quick lanes go on beside it.
// - A drain backfills. The draining job is expected to start once enough running jobs have ended for
//   it to fit, each counted by its learned duration, or by its deadline when nothing is learned of
//   its kind (`drainMs`). In queue order, another development job that fits now starts ahead of it
//   when it too is expected to end by then, or when it takes only units and memory the draining job
//   will leave spare when it starts. The rest wait for it. A job that was already running when the
//   drain began is expected to end at the later of its estimate's end and half as long again as it
//   has run, held to its deadline (`drainEnd`). A job started since the drain began (one backfilled
//   ahead of it) that runs past its estimate is expected at any moment, so once the drain waits on it,
//   nothing more backfills: an overrun delays the drain by at most that job's own deadline, and never
//   compounds. Nothing backfills ahead of a draining job that waits behind take-slot.
// - Backfill trusts only durations learned from a job's own work (low.avin's `trustedDuration`): the
//   daemon gives any other job its deadline as `drainMs`, and every overtaking, ahead of a blocked head
//   or of a drain, counts a job by `drainMs`.
// - Low jobs (low.avin) are decided last, after every take-slot waiter: one starts when it fits and
//   is expected to end before the job that waits (the draining job, or the blocked head) can start,
//   or whenever it fits while nothing waits. One that cannot waits `LowWaits`, is never the head,
//   never drains and keeps no take-slot ticket.
// - An exclusive job owns the machine. While one runs, nothing else starts in any lane: every
//   waiting job waits for it (`ForExclusive`). One that waits never stops a running job; it starts
//   once nothing else runs or starts, nothing ahead of it waits, take-slot holds nothing, and the
//   load has settled when it asked for that (`unsettled`). The first exclusive job in queue order
//   reserves the machine from the moment it queues, its load settled or not: it holds back every job
//   queued behind it, a later quick job and a later exclusive job among them, so no stream of jobs
//   can keep the machine from emptying (it is `Emptying` while marshal's jobs run, whatever the load);
//   the jobs ahead of it are decided as if it and the jobs behind it were not there, and nothing
//   behind it backfills, since it can start only once the machine is empty. Once nothing of
//   marshal's runs, starts or waits and the load still holds it, it is settling (`settles`): it
//   waits for the load alone, however long that takes. Landing jobs are not held back by a waiting
//   exclusive job: one queued, ahead of it or behind, starts first, so a benchmark never delays a
//   release train; only a running exclusive job holds the landing lane.
// - A polite budget (`Budget.fullUnits` above 0; polite.avin) is a part of the full one, admitted
//   against while the user works. Every lane counts against it: a landing or quick job's units are
//   counted beside the development jobs' while it runs, and a landing job starts only when its units
//   fit too, draining the machine for them as it drains for memory. A development or quick job bigger
//   than the polite budget, which fits the full one, runs alone (`Waiting.alone`): the exclusive
//   machinery holds it, so it starts once nothing else of marshal's runs, and nothing starts beside
//   it, but it is niced and settles no load as a development job. A job that fits the full budget
//   beside what runs but not the polite one waits `PoliteBudget`.
//
// The scheduler counts units in quarters (cores.avin) everywhere: a budget's, a job's, take-slot's.
// So a budget of 12 units is 48, and jobs of 0.25 and 1.5 units weigh 1 and 6: whole numbers, which
// add up exactly.

// The units (in quarters) and memory jobs are admitted against. A polite budget also names the full
// one it is a part of (`fullUnits`, `fullMemory`); both are 0 in a budget that is the full one.
data Budget(units: int, memory: long, fullUnits: int = 0, fullMemory: long = 0)

// Whether `b` is a polite budget, a part of the full one.
isPolite(b: Budget) -> bool = b.fullUnits > 0

// How long a development job may wait before the machine drains for it: a job counts as waited once
// `wallNow` (wall-clock microseconds, as `arrived`) is `afterMs` past its arrival, the time it was
// held by hand left out (`waitedMs`).
data Fairness(afterMs: long, wallNow: long)

// No bound: nothing ever drains for a development job.
val Unbounded: Fairness = Fairness(long.MaxValue, 0)

// A job waiting to start, as the scheduler weighs it: `expectedMs` is how long it is expected to run.
// `arrived` is when it was submitted, in microseconds of the wall clock, which is how it is ordered
// against take-slot's waiters.
// `quick` puts it in the quick lane. `drainMs` is how long a drain counts it as running: its learned
// duration, or its deadline when nothing is learned of its kind; 0 counts it by `expectedMs`.
// `exclusive` makes it own the machine; `unsettled`, on an exclusive job, is why it still waits for
// the load to settle (`loadWhy`), None once it need not.
// `alone` says a job bigger than the polite budget runs alone, as an exclusive job does.
// `urgent` says it is in the urgent band: a drain is for it ahead of every job not in the band.
// `low` says it is in the low band (low.avin): it starts only in spare room, never drains the machine
// and holds nothing back; the queue holds it behind every job not low.
// `heldMicros` is how long it was held by hand since `arrived` (holdmany.avin): the drain bound
// leaves it out of the job's wait, while `arrived` keeps its place in the queue.
data Waiting(
    id: long,
    units: int,
    memory: long,
    landing: bool,
    expectedMs: long,
    arrived: long,
    quick: bool = false,
    drainMs: long = 0,
    exclusive: bool = false,
    unsettled: Option[Why] = None,
    alone: bool = false,
    urgent: bool = false,
    low: bool = false,
    heldMicros: long = 0
)

// How long `w` has waited by `wallNow` (wall-clock microseconds) since it joined the queue, the time
// it was held left out, in milliseconds.
waitedMs(w: Waiting, wallNow: long) -> long = (wallNow - w.arrived - w.heldMicros) / 1000

// What a development job that does not fit needs and what is free as the scheduler looks: `units`
// (quarters) and `memory` it needs, `freeUnits` and `freeMemory` beside what runs and starts before
// it, and the running job whose end is expected to let it start (`waitsOn`, 0 where none is, or
// take-slot's runs) and when (`at`, on the clock of `now`; `long.MaxValue` where never).
data Need(units: int, freeUnits: int, memory: long, freeMemory: long, waitsOn: long, at: long)

// Whether `w` owns the machine while it runs: an exclusive job, or one that runs alone.
private owns(w: Waiting) -> bool = w.exclusive || w.alone

// A job running since `startedMs` (the daemon's clock, in milliseconds). `deadlineMs` is how long
// after `startedMs` it is stopped at the latest (its deadline, and any time it spent paused); 0 when
// not known. `exclusive` says it owns the machine, and `alone` that it is bigger than the polite
// budget and runs alone.
data Started(
    id: long,
    units: int,
    memory: long,
    landing: bool,
    startedMs: long,
    expectedMs: long,
    quick: bool = false,
    drainMs: long = 0,
    deadlineMs: long = 0,
    exclusive: bool = false,
    alone: bool = false
)

// Whether a job of a lane counts its units against `budget` while it runs: a development or landing
// job always, a quick job against a polite budget. A landing job starts whatever units the others
// hold, but once it runs what it is charged (`charged`: what it weighs, or what it is measured using
// where that is more) holds back the development jobs after it, as any running job's does.
private counts(budget: Budget, quick: bool) -> bool = isPolite(budget) || !quick

// How long a drain counts a job of `expectedMs` and `drainMs` as running.
private drainEstimate(expectedMs: long, drainMs: long) -> long = if drainMs > 0 then drainMs else expectedMs

// When a running or starting job is expected to end, the units and memory it frees then, and its id
// (0 for take-slot's runs).
type End = (long, int, long, long)

// A take-slot waiter: when it arrived (wall-clock microseconds) and the units it waits for.
data Ticket(arrived: long, units: int)

// What take-slot holds outside marshal: `units` held by its live runs, its live `waiting` tickets,
// and whether one of its runs holds the landing lock.
data Outside(units: int, waiting: Vector[Ticket], landing: bool)

// Nothing outside marshal.
val NoOutside: Outside = Outside(0, [], false)

// The ids of the jobs to start now, in the order to start them: a landing job first, then
// development jobs in queue order.
schedule(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Vector[long] =
  decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).filter(d -> d.why.isEmpty).map(d -> d.id)

// What `schedule` answers, each id with the draining job it starts ahead of when it is backfilled
// during a drain.
starts(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Vector[(long, Option[long])] =
  decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).filter(d -> d.why.isEmpty).map(d -> (d.id, d.ahead))

// The development job the machine drains for and when it is expected to start, on the clock of
// `now`, if one drains and that is known: not while it waits behind take-slot, nor when its units or
// memory never free.
drainStart(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Option[(long, long)] =
  decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).find(d -> d.at.isDefined).map(d -> (d.id, d.at.get))

// The exclusive job that is settling, if one is: its turn has come and nothing of marshal's runs,
// starts or waits, but the load outside marshal has not settled, so it waits for that alone, holding
// the machine as it has since it queued.
settles(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Option[long] =
  decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).find(d -> d.settling).map(d -> d.id)

// What each development job that waits for units or memory needs, and what it waits for (`Need`), in
// the order the scheduler decides them; jobs that wait for anything else are left out.
needs(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Vector[(long, Need)] =
  decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).filter(d -> d.need.isDefined).map(d -> (d.id, d.need.get))

// Each waiting job's place in its lane's queue (from 1) and why it waits, in the order of `queue`:
// what `schedule` would say of it, with `Starting` for a job it would start now.
waits(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside = NoOutside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Vector[(long, int, Why)]
  val decided = decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair)
  val positions = lanePositions(queue)
  val out = Buffer[(long, int, Why)]()
  for (w, position) in queue.zip(positions)
    val why = decided.find(d -> d.id == w.id).flatMap(d -> d.why).getOrElse(Starting)
    out += (w.id, position, why)
  out.toVector

// Each job's place in its own lane's queue (from 1), in the order of `queue`: the landing lane, the
// quick lane and the development jobs each count their own.
lanePositions(queue: Vector[Waiting]) -> Vector[int]
  var landings = 0
  var quicks = 0
  var others = 0
  val out = Buffer[int]()
  for w in queue
    if w.landing
      landings += 1
      out += landings
    elif w.quick
      quicks += 1
      out += quicks
    else
      others += 1
      out += others
  out.toVector

// The ticket the daemon keeps among take-slot's waiters, as (arrival, units), or None when nothing
// of marshal's waits. While a landing job drains the machine, its ticket goes ahead of every
// take-slot waiter, so take-slot admits none of them before it; otherwise the ticket is the first
// development job's, at its arrival, so take-slot's later runs wait behind it: the job the machine
// drains for when there is one (`fair`, `drainTarget`), else the first in queue order.
ticketFor(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside,
    fair: Fairness = Unbounded
) -> Option[(long, int)]
  val drainer = decide(budget, running, queue, now, outside, fair).find(d -> d.why == Some(Draining)).flatMap(
    d -> queue.find(w -> w.id == d.id && w.landing)
  )
  // the jobs behind the first exclusive one wait for it, and take-slot's later runs with them
  val weighed = upToExclusive(queue)
  drainer match
    Some(w) ->
      val first = outside.waiting.map(t -> t.arrived).minOption
      Some((first.filter(a -> a <= w.arrived).map(a -> a - 1).getOrElse(w.arrived), w.units))
    // a low job keeps no ticket: take-slot's runs never wait on its behalf
    None -> drainTarget(weighed, fair).orElse(weighed.find(w -> !w.landing && !w.quick && !w.low)).map(
      w -> (w.arrived, w.units)
    )

// What the scheduler weighs beside `queue`'s first exclusive job (not a landing one), which reserves
// the machine whether or not its load has settled: the queue up to and including it, and every
// landing job. All of `queue` when it has none.
upToExclusive(queue: Vector[Waiting]) -> Vector[Waiting]
  val at = queue.indexWhere(w -> owns(w) && !w.landing)
  if at < 0 then return queue
  queue.take(at + 1) ++ queue.drop(at + 1).filter(w -> w.landing)

// The first development job in queue order that has waited past the bound, if one has. A low job
// never drains the machine: it becomes a normal job once it has waited long enough (low.avin).
waitedPast(queue: Vector[Waiting], fair: Fairness) -> Option[Waiting] =
  queue.find(w -> !w.landing && !w.quick && !w.low && waitedMs(w, fair.wallNow) >= fair.afterMs)

// The development jobs that go ahead of every other once `past` has waited past the bound, in the
// order they go: the urgent band's, in queue order, then `past` (in its place in the band when it is
// urgent itself). None while no job has waited past the bound.
drainOrder(queue: Vector[Waiting], past: Option[Waiting]) -> Vector[Waiting] = past match
  Some(s) ->
    val band = queue.filter(w -> w.urgent && !w.landing && !w.quick)
    if band.exists(w -> w.id == s.id) then band else band ++ [s]
  None -> []

// The development job the machine drains for, once one has waited past the bound, as far as the
// queue alone says: the first in the urgent band when one waits there, which takes the drain over,
// else the job past the bound.
drainTarget(queue: Vector[Waiting], fair: Fairness) -> Option[Waiting] =
  drainOrder(queue, waitedPast(queue, fair)).headOption

// What the scheduler makes of one waiting job: start it now (no `why`), or why it waits. `ahead` is
// the draining job it is backfilled ahead of; `at`, on the draining job, when it is expected to start.
// `settling` says an exclusive job has the machine to itself and waits for the load alone. `need`, on
// a development job that waits for units or memory and on a landing job that drains the machine, is
// what it needs and waits for.
private data Decision(
    id: long,
    why: Option[Why],
    ahead: Option[long] = None,
    at: Option[long] = None,
    settling: bool = false,
    need: Option[Need] = None
)

// The decision for every waiting job: the landing jobs first, then the development jobs in arrival
// order.
private decide(
    budget: Budget,
    running: Vector[Started],
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    outside: Outside,
    fair: Fairness
) -> Vector[Decision]
  val out = Buffer[Decision]()
  // An exclusive job running, or one running alone, holds every lane: whatever waits, waits for it.
  for x in running.find(r -> r.exclusive || r.alone).toList
    for w in queue do out += Decision(w.id, Some(if x.exclusive then ForExclusive(x.id) else ForAlone(x.id)))
    return out.toVector
  val polite = isPolite(budget)
  // The first exclusive job in queue order, or the first to run alone, if one waits; the jobs decided
  // as usual (`weighed`) are those `upToExclusive` names, and take-slot's waiters that arrived before
  // it.
  val exclusive = queue.find(w -> owns(w) && !w.landing)
  val weighed = upToExclusive(queue).filter(w -> exclusive.forall(x -> w.id != x.id))
  val tickets = exclusive.map(x -> outside.waiting.filter(t -> t.arrived < x.arrived)).getOrElse(outside.waiting)
  // When each running or starting job is expected to end, with the units and memory it frees and its
  // id (0 for take-slot's runs).
  val ends = Buffer[End]()
  // the same, each job counted as a drain counts it (`drainMs`)
  val sure = Buffer[End]()
  var memory: long = 0
  var laneBusy = outside.landing
  var units = outside.units
  // the units take-slot's runs hold, and its waiters that fit are to hold
  var theirs = outside.units
  if outside.units > 0
    ends += (now, outside.units, 0, 0)
    sure += (now, outside.units, 0, 0)
  var quicks = 0
  // Once a job has waited past the bound, the jobs that go first (`drainOrder`): the urgent band's
  // development jobs, then it; the first of them that does not fit is the one the machine drains
  // for. And when on the daemon's clock the drain began: when the job past the bound waited past it.
  val past = waitedPast(weighed, fair)
  val first = drainOrder(weighed, past)
  val began = past.map(s -> now - (waitedMs(s, fair.wallNow) - fair.afterMs)).getOrElse(long.MinValue)
  for r in running
    if r.landing then laneBusy = true
    elif r.quick then quicks += 1
    val frees = if counts(budget, r.quick) then r.units else 0
    units += frees
    memory += r.memory
    ends += (expectedEnd(r.startedMs, r.expectedMs, now), frees, r.memory, r.id)
    sure += (drainEnd(r, now, began), frees, r.memory, r.id)
  // the landing job that waits for memory and drains the machine, if one does
  var draining: Option[long] = None
  for w in queue.filter(w -> w.landing)
    if laneBusy
      out += Decision(w.id, Some(if outside.landing then ForTakeSlot else LaneBusy))
    elif draining.isDefined
      out += Decision(w.id, draining.map(id -> Behind(id)))
    elif (memory + w.memory <= budget.memory && (!polite || units + w.units <= budget.units)) || running.isEmpty
      out += Decision(w.id, None)
      laneBusy = true
      memory += w.memory
      // what it weighs holds back the development jobs decided after it
      val taken = w.units
      units += taken
      ends += (now + w.expectedMs, taken, w.memory, w.id)
      sure += (now + drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs), taken, w.memory, w.id)
    else
      // it waits for memory (and, polite, units) to free: what it needs, and the running job whose
      // end is expected to let it start, as a development job's drain says them
      val needUnits = if polite then w.units else 0
      val (at, id) = whenFitsBy(budget, if polite then units else 0, memory, needUnits, w.memory, sure)
      val need = Need(needUnits, budget.units - (if polite then units else 0), w.memory, budget.memory - memory, id, at)
      out += Decision(w.id, Some(Draining), need = Some(need))
      draining = Some(w.id)
  // While a landing job drains the machine, every development job waits behind it and no take-slot
  // waiter is counted as admitted.
  for id in draining.toList
    for w in queue.filter(w -> !w.landing)
      out += Decision(w.id, Some(Behind(id)))
    return out.toVector
  val quick = quickLane(budget, weighed, now, quicks, memory, ends, sure, out)
  memory = quick.0
  units += quick.1
  // When the blocked head of the queue can start, and which job it is (None for a take-slot
  // waiter); None while the head has not been met.
  var head: Option[(long, Option[long])] = None
  // Those jobs go first; the first of them that does not fit drains the machine, and the development
  // jobs after it wait for it (`hold`).
  val order = first ++ weighed.filter(w -> !first.exists(f -> f.id == w.id))
  var hold: Option[long] = None
  // While the machine drains: whether jobs may backfill, when the draining job is expected to
  // start, and the units and memory it leaves spare then.
  var backfills = false
  var drainAt: long = 0
  var spareUnits = 0
  var spareMemory: long = 0
  for e in arrivalOrder(order, tickets)
    // A low job starts only where it delays no job that is not low: whenever it fits while nothing
    // else waits, and otherwise only when it fits and is expected to end before the job that waits
    // can start, the draining job or the blocked head (`drainEstimate`: a duration learned from its
    // own work, else its deadline). It never becomes the head nor drains, so it holds nothing back.
    if e.job.exists(w -> w.low)
      val w = e.job.get
      val fits = units + w.units <= budget.units && memory + w.memory <= budget.memory
      val estimate = drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs)
      val until = if hold.isDefined then (if backfills then drainAt else now) else head.map(h -> h.0).getOrElse(
        long.MaxValue
      )
      if fits && (until == long.MaxValue || (until > now && estimate <= until - now))
        units += w.units
        memory += w.memory
        ends += (now + w.expectedMs, w.units, w.memory, w.id)
        sure += (now + estimate, w.units, w.memory, w.id)
        out += Decision(w.id, None, hold)
      else
        out += Decision(w.id, Some(LowWaits))
      continue
    if hold.isDefined
      for w in e.job.toList
        val fits = units + w.units <= budget.units && memory + w.memory <= budget.memory
        val estimate = drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs)
        val endsFirst = drainAt > now && estimate <= drainAt - now
        val spare = w.units <= spareUnits && w.memory <= spareMemory
        if backfills && fits && (endsFirst || spare)
          units += w.units
          memory += w.memory
          ends += (now + w.expectedMs, w.units, w.memory, w.id)
          sure += (now + estimate, w.units, w.memory, w.id)
          if !endsFirst
            spareUnits -= w.units
            spareMemory -= w.memory
          out += Decision(w.id, None, hold)
        else
          out += Decision(w.id, hold.map(id -> DrainingFor(id)))
      continue
    val fits = units + e.units <= budget.units && memory + e.memory <= budget.memory
    // how long a job is counted as running when it would overtake the blocked head: a duration
    // learned from its own work, else its deadline (`drainMs`), as a drain counts it
    val overtakes = e.job.map(w -> drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs)).getOrElse(e.expectedMs)
    val go = head match
      None ->
        if !fits then head = Some((whenFits(budget, units, memory, e.units, e.memory, ends), e.job.map(w -> w.id)))
        fits
      // take-slot never lets a waiter overtake; a marshal job may, when it delays nobody
      Some((at, _)) -> e.job.isDefined && fits && now + overtakes <= at
    if go
      units += e.units
      memory += e.memory
      ends += (now + e.expectedMs, e.units, e.memory, e.job.map(w -> w.id).getOrElse(0))
      // an urgent job that starts ahead of the job the machine drains for is counted by the drain
      // too, so when the drain ends is known in the same look
      for w in e.job.toList do sure += (now + drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs), w.units, w.memory, w.id)
      if e.job.isEmpty then theirs += e.units
    for w in e.job.toList
      if go
        out += Decision(w.id, None)
      elif first.exists(f -> f.id == w.id)
        hold = Some(w.id)
        val why = drainingFor(waitsFor(budget, units, memory, theirs, e, fits, head))
        // it is the head itself, waiting for units or memory to free: others may backfill
        if why == Draining && head.exists(h -> h.1 == Some(w.id))
          drainAt = whenFits(budget, units, memory, e.units, e.memory, sure)
          if drainAt < long.MaxValue
            backfills = true
            val free = freeAt(budget, units, memory, sure, drainAt)
            spareUnits = free.0 - e.units
            spareMemory = free.1 - e.memory
        val need = if fits then None else Some(needOf(budget, units, memory, e, sure))
        out += Decision(w.id, Some(why), None, if backfills then Some(drainAt) else None, need = need)
      else
        val need = if fits then None else Some(needOf(budget, units, memory, e, ends))
        out += Decision(w.id, Some(waitsFor(budget, units, memory, theirs, e, fits, head)), need = need)
  for x in exclusive.toList
    // it waits behind a job ahead of it that waits, then for the machine to empty (holding back what
    // is behind it all along, its load settled or not); one whose load has not settled once the
    // machine is empty and nothing else waits settles: it waits for the load alone
    val ahead = out.find(d -> d.why.isDefined && weighed.exists(w -> w.id == d.id && !w.landing))
    // take-slot's waiters that arrived before it go before it, as take-slot admits them
    val busy = running.nonEmpty || out.exists(
      d -> d.why.isEmpty
    ) || outside.units > 0 || outside.landing || tickets.nonEmpty
    val free = ahead.isEmpty && !busy
    if x.unsettled.isDefined && free then out += Decision(x.id, x.unsettled, settling = true)
    else
      val why = if ahead.isDefined then ahead.map(
        d -> Behind(d.id)
      ) elif busy then Some(if x.exclusive then Emptying else RunsAlone) else None
      out += Decision(x.id, why)
    for w in queue
      if !w.landing && w.id != x.id && !weighed.exists(v -> v.id == w.id) then out += Decision(
        w.id,
        Some(if x.exclusive then ForExclusive(x.id) else ForAlone(x.id))
      )
  out.toVector

// Decides the quick lane's jobs into `out`, `quicks` of them running, beside `memory` in use, and
// answers the memory in use after them: what the quick jobs it starts take, and what the first one
// that waits for memory keeps from the development jobs; and the units the jobs it starts take
// from a polite budget (none from a full one).
private quickLane(
    budget: Budget,
    queue: Vector[Waiting],
    now: long,
    quicks: int,
    memory: long,
    ends: Buffer[End],
    sure: Buffer[End],
    out: Buffer[Decision]
) -> (long, int)
  var free = QuickSlots - quicks
  var used = memory
  var units = 0
  var blocked: Option[long] = None
  for w in queue.filter(w -> w.quick && !w.landing)
    if blocked.isDefined
      out += Decision(w.id, blocked.map(id -> Behind(id)))
    elif free <= 0
      out += Decision(w.id, Some(QuickFull))
    elif used + w.memory <= budget.memory
      out += Decision(w.id, None)
      free -= 1
      used += w.memory
      val taken = if counts(budget, true) then w.units else 0
      units += taken
      ends += (now + w.expectedMs, taken, w.memory, w.id)
      sure += (now + drainEstimate(w.expectedMs, w.drainMs), taken, w.memory, w.id)
    else
      out += Decision(
        w.id,
        Some(if isPolite(budget) && used + w.memory <= budget.fullMemory then PoliteBudget else NoMemory)
      )
      blocked = Some(w.id)
      used += w.memory
  (used, units)

// Why `e` waits. One that does not fit beside `used` units and `memory` waits for units, unless they
// would fit but for what take-slot's runs and admitted waiters hold (`theirs`), or else for memory. One that fits waits
// behind the blocked head, a job or a take-slot waiter. Against a polite budget, one that would fit
// beside what runs in the full budget waits for the polite one (`PoliteBudget`).
private waitsFor(
    budget: Budget,
    used: int,
    memory: long,
    theirs: int,
    e: Entry,
    fits: bool,
    head: Option[(long, Option[long])]
) -> Why
  if fits then return head match
    Some((_, Some(id))) -> Behind(id)
    _ -> ForTakeSlot
  val roomy = isPolite(budget) && used + e.units <= budget.fullUnits && memory + e.memory <= budget.fullMemory
  if used + e.units > budget.units
    if used - theirs + e.units <= budget.units then return ForTakeSlot
    return if roomy then PoliteBudget else NoUnits
  if roomy then PoliteBudget else NoMemory

// Why the job the machine drains for waits: `draining` while it waits for units or memory to free,
// and otherwise what it waits for (take-slot).
private drainingFor(why: Why) -> Why
drainingFor(NoUnits) = Draining
drainingFor(NoMemory) = Draining
drainingFor(PoliteBudget) = Draining
drainingFor(why) = why

// When a drain that began at `began` counts the running job `r` as ending.
// - A job already running as the drain began is expected to end at the later of the end of its
//   estimate (`drainMs`) and half as long again as it has run so far (`now + elapsed / 2`), held to its
//   deadline: a job well into its run is not expected to end the moment its estimate passes, nor to
//   use its whole deadline. A deadline already passed counts as now (the job is being stopped).
// - A job started since (backfilled ahead of the drain, or a landing or quick job) is expected at the
//   end of its estimate, and once past it at any moment, so an overrun delays the drain by at most
//   that job's own deadline and delays never compound.
private drainEnd(r: Started, now: long, began: long) -> long
  val end = r.startedMs + drainEstimate(r.expectedMs, r.drainMs)
  if r.startedMs >= began then return if end > now then end else now
  val elapsed = if now > r.startedMs then now - r.startedMs else 0
  val realistic = if end > now + elapsed / 2 then end else now + elapsed / 2
  if r.deadlineMs <= 0 then return realistic
  val latest = r.startedMs + r.deadlineMs
  if latest <= now then now elif realistic < latest then realistic else latest

// A running job past its expected end may end at any moment: it is expected now.
private expectedEnd(startedMs: long, expectedMs: long, now: long) -> long =
  if startedMs + expectedMs > now then startedMs + expectedMs else now

// A development job (`job`) or a take-slot waiter (no job, expected to end at once) in the queue.
private data Entry(job: Option[Waiting], units: int, memory: long, expectedMs: long)

// The development jobs of `queue` and take-slot's `tickets` in one arrival order; a ticket goes first
// on a tie. Low jobs come after every ticket, as they come after every job not low.
private arrivalOrder(queue: Vector[Waiting], tickets: Vector[Ticket]) -> Vector[Entry]
  val sorted = tickets.sortBy(t -> t.arrived)
  val out = Buffer[Entry]()
  var t = 0
  for w in queue
    if w.landing || w.quick then continue
    while t < sorted.length && (w.low || sorted(t).arrived <= w.arrived)
      out += Entry(None, sorted(t).units, 0, 0)
      t += 1
    out += Entry(Some(w), w.units, w.memory, w.expectedMs)
  while t < sorted.length
    out += Entry(None, sorted(t).units, 0, 0)
    t += 1
  out.toVector

// The earliest time `units` and `memory` more fit, if the jobs in `ends` end when they are expected to.
private whenFits(
    budget: Budget,
    used: int,
    memory: long,
    units: int,
    needs: long,
    ends: Buffer[End]
) -> long = whenFitsBy(budget, used, memory, units, needs, ends).0

// The same, with the id of the job whose end is expected to make them fit (0 for take-slot's runs, or
// where they never fit).
private whenFitsBy(
    budget: Budget,
    used: int,
    memory: long,
    units: int,
    needs: long,
    ends: Buffer[End]
) -> (long, long)
  var freeUnits = budget.units - used
  var freeMemory = budget.memory - memory
  for (at, u, m, id) in ends.sortBy(e -> e.0)
    freeUnits += u
    freeMemory += m
    if units <= freeUnits && needs <= freeMemory then return (at, id)
  (long.MaxValue, 0)

// What the job of `e` needs beside `used` units and `memory`, and the job in `ends` whose end is
// expected to let it start, and when.
private needOf(budget: Budget, used: int, memory: long, e: Entry, ends: Buffer[End]) -> Need
  val (at, id) = whenFitsBy(budget, used, memory, e.units, e.memory, ends)
  Need(e.units, budget.units - used, e.memory, budget.memory - memory, id, at)

// The units and memory free at `at`, beside `used` units and `memory` now, if the jobs in `ends` end
// when they are expected to.
private freeAt(budget: Budget, used: int, memory: long, ends: Buffer[End], at: long) -> (int, long)
  var freeUnits = budget.units - used
  var freeMemory = budget.memory - memory
  for (t, u, m, _) in ends
    if t <= at
      freeUnits += u
      freeMemory += m
  (freeUnits, freeMemory)

// Why a job can never start under `budget`, or None when it can. A landing job of any size can: one
// whose memory exceeds the budget starts when nothing else runs.
neverFits(budget: Budget, units: int, memory: long, landing: bool) -> Option[string]
  if units < 1 then return Some(s"a job weighs at least 0.25 units, not ${formatUnits(units)}")
  if memory < 0 then return Some("a job's memory is not negative")
  if landing then return None
  if units > budget.units then return Some(
    s"the job needs ${formatUnits(units)} units and the budget is ${formatUnits(budget.units)}"
  )
  if memory > budget.memory then return Some(
    s"the job needs ${formatSize(memory)} of memory and the budget is ${formatSize(budget.memory)}"
  )
  None

// The units a job of `kind` weighs, in quarters, when it does not say and nothing is learned of its
// command: a test 4, anything else 1.
defaultUnits(kind: string) -> int = wholeUnits(if kind == "test" then 4 else 1)

// The `nice` level a development job, and a quick one, is started under.
val DevelopmentNice: int = 15

// The `nice` level a job is started under, however it starts (in its turn, or backfilled ahead of a
// draining job): 0, not niced, for a landing job, an exclusive one and one in the urgent band as it
// starts (`--urgent`, or moved there by `priority`), since each is work the machine is waiting on;
// `LowNice` for one in the low band as it starts (low.avin); `DevelopmentNice` for every other job.
niceFor(landing: bool, exclusive: bool, urgent: bool, low: bool = false) -> int =
  if landing || exclusive || urgent then 0 elif low then LowNice else DevelopmentNice
